From: Erick Fuentes <fuentes.erick@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix make_iterator return type under pybind11 2.12+

pybind11 2.12 changed make_iterator to return typing::Iterator<T>
instead of a plain py::iterator, so the two return statements in the
RosValue __iter__ lambda now deduce different types and the lambda no
longer compiles:

  error: return type 'Iterator<const pybind11::str>' must match previous
  return type 'Iterator<const pybind11::object>' when lambda expression
  has unspecified explicit return type

typing::Iterator<T> derives from py::iterator, so naming py::iterator as
the explicit return type restores a single common type. The other
make_iterator lambdas each have one return statement and are unaffected.
---
 python/embag.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/python/embag.cc b/python/embag.cc
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/python/embag.cc
+++ b/python/embag.cc
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ PYBIND11_MODULE(embag, m) {
         py::arg("array_blob_types") = default_array_blob_types,
         py::arg("blob_types_as_memoryview") = false,
         py::arg("ros_time_py_type") = py::none())
-      .def("__iter__", [](Embag::RosValue::Pointer &v) {
+      .def("__iter__", [](Embag::RosValue::Pointer &v) -> py::iterator {
         switch (v->getType()) {
           case Embag::RosValue::Type::array:
           case Embag::RosValue::Type::primitive_array:
--
